pokeplatinum-portc.patch (tools/pokeplat_gen.py applies it to build/pokeplatinum): pret's C that Metrowerks accepts and the
port's clang (64-bit host, C) does not, each as the smallest edit:
- lvalue casts `(u8 *)p += n;` (9: pc_boxes/application_manager.c, overlay005/ov5_021ECE40.c, main_menu/ov97_02232DC8.c)
- struct assignment of a struct with a const member (overlay_manager.c: memcpy)
- `\uNNNN` escapes of Shift-JIS bytes in four debug strings (underground/comm_manager.c): clang refuses UCNs of control
  characters; `\xNN` is the byte MWCC makes
- initializers holding function addresses as u32 (applications/bag/main.c, underground/menus.c, underground/player_talk.c):
  not constant on a 64-bit host; uintptr_t is (the consumers still pass these through u32: the pointer pass)
- implicit declarations, which on x86-64 return int (a pointer would be cut to 32 bits): the missing #include
  (heap.h, graphics.h, wifi_history_save_data.h, chatot_cry.h, underground/manager.h), include/link_contest_records.h
  guarded with contest.h's name (so contest.c never saw it), and prototypes for functions defined in one .c and called from
  another with no header (PlayerAvatar_GetMoveState, BattleController_EmitSelected*, PokedexSort_NumDisplayed,
  CapsuleGraphics_LoadBgLayer2Tilemap/Dummy)

